# Grid B — U1 Security audit (command injection surface)
#
# Gap target: no security_audit scenario exists (see scenario.go
# comments referencing aspirational security_audit / refactor_design
# that were never wired). This case measures whether the pipeline
# can reach a taint-source → sink answer via the architecture_explain
# fallback path.
#
# Ground truth (internal/tool/builtin.go:108): ExecCommand.Execute
# shells out via the exec_command tool. The relevant audit question
# is whether user input paths can reach exec_command without
# sanitization, and the known defense is that REPL requests are
# passed as --request arg, not into a shell pipeline.
#
# Positive anchor pins the tool name the audit must be scoped to.
# Negative anchors block the "no risk" brush-off and the opposite
# "sql injection" hallucination from training-distribution leakage
# (codrax has no database).
ID="u1a"
NAME="security audit — exec_command injection surface"
QUESTION="codrax 的 exec_command 工具是否存在命令注入风险？请给出实际的 taint source 和 sink，以及现有的防护点。"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="exec_command"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="no.risk SQL.injection sql"
